1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,480
Salahdine Parnasse against Ilia Topuria.

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:04,700
It is the matchup suddenly getting attention,

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,780
and there is more behind the conversation

4
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:08,420
than a random fan poster.

5
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:10,840
Parnasse's coach has shared a revealing message,

6
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:14,380
and RMC Sport reports that Parnasse reposted

7
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:15,640
a TikTok about the fight.

8
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,980
But the same message contains the detail

9
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:19,500
that changes the whole story:

10
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:20,780
nothing is signed.

11
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:22,800
Here is what those signals actually tell

12
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:23,100
us.

13
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,840
ActuMMA describes two Instagram stories from

14
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:28,085
Stéphane Chaufourier,

15
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:29,573
better known as Atch,

16
00:00:29,573 --> 00:00:31,240
Parnasse's coach and manager.

17
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,060
The first is a short,

18
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:34,120
cryptic message:

19
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:37,060
“La Parnassa.” The screenshot names neither

20
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:38,320
an opponent nor a date.

21
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:39,540
On its own,

22
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:40,280
that is a tease.

23
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:42,680
It does not establish that Topuria has

24
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:43,240
been approached,

25
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:45,360
that negotiations are taking place,

26
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,480
or that the UFC has chosen this

27
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:48,560
matchup for a card.

28
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:50,940
The second story is much more useful.

29
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,560
Atch reshared a message from MMA Gang

30
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:55,880
saying that he and Parnasse would not

31
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:57,010
turn down the matchup.

32
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:58,860
Its wording is conditional:

33
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:02,080
if the UFC wants Topuria against Salah,

34
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:03,820
the answer would be a big yes.

35
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:06,120
That is an expression of interest from

36
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:07,140
Parnasse's side.

37
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:08,760
It is not a statement that both

38
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:09,660
fighters have agreed,

39
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:11,620
and it is not an announcement from

40
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:12,100
the promotion.

41
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,420
Then comes the line that should stay

42
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:16,560
attached to every headline about this story.

43
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,260
The reshared message says there is no

44
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:20,260
signature and,

45
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:20,880
above all,

46
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:21,560
nothing official.

47
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:25,000
Those are not caveats added by somebody

48
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:25,900
outside the camp.

49
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:28,060
They are in the very post generating

50
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:28,940
the excitement.

51
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:31,060
Removing that sentence turns a willingness

52
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:32,420
to fight into a booking,

53
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:34,260
which is a much stronger claim than

54
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:35,680
the available evidence supports.

55
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:37,740
There is also the TikTok angle.

56
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:40,359
In its report published on October fifth,

57
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:43,620
RMC Sport says Parnasse reposted a TikTok

58
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:45,640
announcing a future fight with Topuria.

59
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:48,300
We have not independently verified the original

60
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:51,020
repost, so that detail is attributed to

61
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:51,540
RMC.

62
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:53,820
Even if the repost is exactly as

63
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:56,420
described, sharing somebody else's video still

64
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:58,140
does not establish a signed agreement.

65
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:00,320
It makes his interest more visible,

66
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:02,340
without settling the booking question.

67
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:04,900
RMC also explains why this pairing has

68
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:05,240
traction.

69
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,880
Its report says Parnasse made a striking

70
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:11,180
UFC debut in Paris on September fifth,

71
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:13,180
stopping Dan Hooker in two minutes and

72
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:14,260
thirty-five seconds.

73
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:16,540
Afterward, he called for a top-five opponent

74
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:18,100
and mentioned Max Holloway.

75
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:20,120
In that context,

76
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:22,740
a message welcoming Topuria fits the direction

77
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:24,520
his camp is publicly discussing:

78
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:27,020
a bigger test after an impressive first

79
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:27,460
appearance.

80
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:29,720
There is a reason the proposed opponent

81
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:30,400
matters.

82
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:33,560
RMC lists Topuria as the number-one lightweight

83
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:35,460
and Parnasse as number nine.

84
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:37,740
Those rankings are reported context,

85
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:39,420
not proof of the next fight.

86
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:41,860
They explain why the rumor feels like

87
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:43,446
an ambitious step for Parnasse.

88
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:45,920
A high-profile opponent would test him against

89
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:47,600
a very different level of expectation,

90
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:50,460
while a social-media tease alone tells us

91
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:52,320
little about whether that step will happen

92
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:52,680
next.

93
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:56,120
The timing circulating with this story is

94
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:58,820
January, with RMC mentioning rumors around

95
00:02:58,820 --> 00:02:59,978
UFC three thirty-six.

96
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:03,340
That should remain labeled as rumor.

97
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,600
The screenshots do not provide a signed

98
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:06,700
date, a venue,

99
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:08,840
or a confirmed place on that card.

100
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:11,280
There is also no acceptance from Topuria

101
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:12,720
established by these posts.

102
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,900
The headline can ask whether the fight

103
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:15,540
is possible;

104
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:18,000
it cannot responsibly present the card and

105
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,100
the opponent as settled.

106
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,360
The next meaningful update would be an

107
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,940
explicit announcement from the UFC,

108
00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:25,400
or a clear confirmation of an agreement

109
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:26,520
from the people involved.

110
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,840
More fan edits and more reposts can

111
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:29,580
increase attention,

112
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:31,460
but they do not answer the missing

113
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:32,020
questions.

114
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:33,860
Has an offer been made?

115
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,340
Have both sides accepted?

116
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:36,500
What is the date?

117
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:37,500
At the moment,

118
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,880
the public message establishes enthusiasm from

119
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:42,200
Parnasse's camp while leaving those booking

120
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:43,180
details unresolved.

121
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:45,120
So the development is real,

122
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:47,640
but narrower than some headlines suggest.

123
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:50,660
Atch has amplified a message welcoming the

124
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:51,020
matchup.

125
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:54,028
RMC reports a TikTok repost from Parnasse.

126
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:56,360
And the camp's own message says nothing

127
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:57,600
is signed or official.

128
00:03:58,200 --> 00:03:59,940
That combination makes this a story to

129
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:01,840
follow, rather than a fight to put

130
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:02,900
on a confirmed schedule.

131
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,840
Would you want Parnasse to take this

132
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:05,600
challenge next?

133
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,060
Drop your thoughts below.
